{
  "total": 82,
  "totalPage": 2,
  "page": 2,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cbff",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2583,
      "bookHadithIndex": 51,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W.) said:“May Allah curse the thief! He steals an egg and his hand is cut off, and he steals a rope and his hand is cut off”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2583-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2583-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2583-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2583-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc00",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2584,
      "bookHadithIndex": 52,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Umar said:“The Prophet (S.A.W.) cut off (the hand of a thief) for a shield worth three Dirham.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2584-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2584-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2584-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2584-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc01",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2585,
      "bookHadithIndex": 53,
      "text": "It was narrated from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W.) said:“Do not cut off (the thief's hand) except for something worth one quarter of a Dinar or more",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2585-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2585-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2585-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc02",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2586,
      "bookHadithIndex": 54,
      "text": "It was narrated from Amir bin Sa'd, from this father, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“The hand of the thief is to be cut off for the price of a shield",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2586-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2586-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2586-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc03",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2587,
      "bookHadithIndex": 55,
      "text": "It was narrated that Ibn Muhairiz said:“I asked Fadalah bin Ubaid about hanging the hand (of the thief) from this neck, and he said: 'It is sunnah. The messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cut off a man's hand then hung it from his neck",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2587-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2587-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2587-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2587-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc04",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2588,
      "bookHadithIndex": 56,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abdur-Rahman bin Tha’labah Al-Ansari, from his father, that Amr bin Samurah bin Habib bin Abd Shams came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said:“O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! I stole a camel belonging to Banu so-and-so; purify me!” The Prophet (ﷺ) sent word to them and they said: “(Yes), we have lost a camel of ours.” So the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered that his hand be cut off. Tha'labah said: “I was looking at him when his hand fell and he said (to it) 'Praise is to Allah (STW) Who has purified me of you; you wanted to cause my whole body to enter Hell",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2588-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2588-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2588-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2588-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc05",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2589,
      "bookHadithIndex": 57,
      "text": "It was narrated Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“If a slave steals, then sell him, even for half Price.' ”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2589-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2589-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2589-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2589-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc06",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2590,
      "bookHadithIndex": 58,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas that :one of the slaves of Khumus stole something from the Khumus, and the matter was referred to the Prophet (ﷺ) but he did not cut off his hand, and he said ' The Property of Allah, (STW) part of it stealing another part.' ”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2590-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2590-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2590-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2590-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc07",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2591,
      "bookHadithIndex": 59,
      "text": "It was narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The hand of the one who betrays a trust, the robber and the pilferer is not to be cut off”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2591-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2591-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2591-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2591-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc08",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2592,
      "bookHadithIndex": 60,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibrahim bin Abdur-Rahman bin Awf that his father said:“I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'The hand of the pilferer is not to be cut off”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2592-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2592-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2592-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2592-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc09",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2593,
      "bookHadithIndex": 61,
      "text": "It was narrated from Rafi bin Khadij that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2593-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2593-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2593-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2593-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc0a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2594,
      "bookHadithIndex": 62,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The hand is not to be cut off for (stealing) produce or the spadix of palm trees.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2594-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2594-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2594-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc0b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2595,
      "bookHadithIndex": 63,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abdullah bin Safwan that :his father slept in the mosque, using his upper wrap as a pillow, and it was taken from beneath his head. He brought the thief to the Prophet (ﷺ) and the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered that his hand be cut off. Safwan said: “O Messenger of Allah , (ﷺ) I did not want this! I give my upper wrap to him in charity.” The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Why did you not give it to him before you brought him to me?”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2595-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2595-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2595-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2595-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc0c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2596,
      "bookHadithIndex": 64,
      "text": "XOIt was narrated from Amr bin Shu'aib, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man from Muzainah asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about fruits. :He said: “What is taken from the tree and carried away, its value and the like of it along with it (meaning double its price must be paid). What (is taken) from the place where dates are dried, (the penalty) is cutting off the hand if the amount taken is equal to the price of a shield. But if (the person) eats it and does not take it away, there is no penalty.” He said: “What about the sheep taken from the pasture, O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?” He said: “(The thief) must pay double its price and be punished, and if it was in the pen then his hand should be cut off, if what was taken was worth the price of a shield.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2596-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2596-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2596-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2596-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc0d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2597,
      "bookHadithIndex": 65,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ishaq bin Abu Talhah:“I heard Abu Mundhir, the freed slave of Abu Dharr, say that Abu Umayyah narrated to him, that a thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he admitted his crime, although the stolen goods were not found with him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'I do not think you stole them.’ He said: 'Yes I did.' Then he said (again): ‘I do not think that you stole them.’ and he said: 'Yes I did.' Then he ordered that his hand be cut off. The Prophet (ﷺ) ' Say: I seek Allah's forgiveness and I repent to Him.' So he (the thief) said: 'I seek Allah's forgiveness and I repent to him.' He (the Prophet (ﷺ) said twice: 'O Allah! Accept his repentance.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2597-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2597-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2597-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc0e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2598,
      "bookHadithIndex": 66,
      "text": "It was narrated from 'Abdul Jabbar bin Wa'il that his father said:“A Woman was coerced (i.e., raped) during the time of Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) He waived the legal punishment for her and carried it out on the one who had attacked her, but he (the narrator) did not say that he rules that she should be given a bridal-money.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2598-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2598-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2598-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2598-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc0f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2599,
      "bookHadithIndex": 67,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Do not carry out the legal punishment in the mosque.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2599-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2599-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2599-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc10",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2600,
      "bookHadithIndex": 68,
      "text": "Amr bin Shu'aib narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that:the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade lashing for the legal punishment in the mosques",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2600-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2600-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2600-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2600-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc11",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2601,
      "bookHadithIndex": 69,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Burdah bin Niyar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say:“No one should be given more than ten lashes, except in the case of one of the legal punishments of Allah (SWT).”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2601-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2601-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2601-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2601-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc12",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2602,
      "bookHadithIndex": 70,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Do not punish with more than ten whips.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2602-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2602-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2602-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Very Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2602-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc13",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2603,
      "bookHadithIndex": 71,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ubadah bin Samit that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever among you undergoes a Hadd, his punishment has been brought forward, and it is an expiation for him otherwise his case rests with Allah.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2603-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2603-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2603-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2603-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc14",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2604,
      "bookHadithIndex": 72,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ali that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, Allah (STW) is too just to repeat the punishment for his slave (in the hereafter). And whoever commits a sin in this world and Allah conceals him, Allah is too generous to go back to something that He has pardoned.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2604-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2604-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2604-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc15",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2605,
      "bookHadithIndex": 73,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that Sa'd bin Ubadah Al-Ansari said:“O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) if a man finds another man with his wife, should he kill him?” The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “No.” Sa'd said: “Yes he should, by the one who honored you with the Truth!” The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Listen to what your leader says!”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2605-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2605-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2605-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2605-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc16",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2606,
      "bookHadithIndex": 74,
      "text": "It was narrated that Salamah bin Muhabbiq said:“When the Verse of legal punishments was revealed, it was said to Abu Thabit Sa'd bin Ubadah, who was a jealous man: ‘If you found another man with your wife, what would you do?’ He said: “I would strike them both wife the sword; do you think I should wait until I bring four (witness) and he has satisfied himself and gone away? Or should I say I saw such and such, and you will carry out the legal punishment punishment on me (for slander) and never accept my testimony thereafter?' Mention of that was made to the prophet (ﷺ) and he said: “The sword is sufficient as a witness.' Then he said: 'No (on second thought) I am afraid that the drunkard and the jealous would pursue that.” (Da'if) Abu Abdullah - meaning Ibn Majah - said: “I heard Abu Zurah saying: “This is a Hadith of Ali bin Muhammad At-Tanafisi, I did not hear it from him.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2606-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2606-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2606-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2606-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc17",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2607,
      "bookHadithIndex": 75,
      "text": "It was narrated that Bara bin Azib said:“My maternal uncle passed by me - (one of the narrators) Hushaim named him in his narration as Harith bin Amr - and the Prophet (ﷺ) had given him a banner to carry. I said to him: 'Where are you going?’ He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has sent me to a man who married his father's wife after he died, and has commanded me to strike his neck (i.e. execute him).”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2607-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2607-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2607-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc18",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2608,
      "bookHadithIndex": 76,
      "text": "It was narrated from Mu'awiyah bin Qurrah that his father said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to a man who had married his father's wife after he died, to strike his neck (execute him) and confiscate his wealth.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2608-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2608-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2608-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc19",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2609,
      "bookHadithIndex": 77,
      "text": "It was narrated from Ibn Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father, or (a freed slave) who claims that his Wala is for other than his real master, the curse of Allah (SWT), the angels and all the people will be upon him.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2609-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2609-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2609-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc1a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2610,
      "bookHadithIndex": 78,
      "text": "It was narrated that Abu Uthman Nahdi said:“I heard Sa'd and Abu Bakrah both say that they heard directly from Muhammad (ﷺ) saying it and memorized: 'Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father knowing the he is not his father, Paradise will be forbidden to him.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2610-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2610-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2610-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2610-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc1b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2611,
      "bookHadithIndex": 79,
      "text": "It was narrated from Abdullah bin Amr that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, even though its fragrance may be detected from a distance of five hundred years.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2611-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2611-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2611-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc1c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2612,
      "bookHadithIndex": 80,
      "text": "Muslim bin Haisam narrated from Ash'ath bin Qais who said:“I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with a delegation from Kindah, and they thought that I was the best of them. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) are you not from among us?' He said: 'We are the tribe of Banu Nadr bin Kinanah, and we do not attribute ourselves to our mother and we do not deny our forefathers.'”He said: “Ash'ath bin Qais used to say: 'If any man is brought to me who suggests that a man from Quraish does not belong to Nadr bin Kinanah, I would carry out the legal punishment (for slander) on him.'”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2612-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2612-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2612-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2612-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc1d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2613,
      "bookHadithIndex": 81,
      "text": "Safwan bin Umayyah said:“We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and Amr bin Murrah came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), Allah (SWT) has decreed that I be doomed, and He has not guided me to earn a living except by beating my tambourine with my hand; give me permission to sing without doing anything immoral.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'I will not give you permission, or honor you nor give you, what you want. You are lying, O enemy of Allah. Allah (SWT) has granted you a good, lawful provision, but you have chosen the provision that Allah (SWT) has forbidden to you instead of that which He has permitted. If I had warned you before, I would have done such and such to you. Get away from me and repent to Allah (SWT). If you do that again, after this warning, I will give you a painful beating and shave your head, to make an example of you, and I will banish you from among your people, and tell the young men of Al-Madinah to come and take your goods,'Amr stood up, suffering grief and humiliation that is known only to Allah (SWT). When he went away, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Those sinners, whoever among them dies without having repented, Allah (SWT) will gather him on the Day of Resurrection just as he was in this world, effeminate and naked, with not even a piece of cloth to conceal him from the people. Every time he gets up, he will fall to the ground.'”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2613-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2613-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2613-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Mawdu"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2613-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c88cdd1a4c9c86f0cc1e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324",
      "bookIndex": 20,
      "hadithIndex": 2614,
      "bookHadithIndex": 82,
      "text": "It was narrated from Umm Salamah that :the Prophet (ﷺ) entered upon her, and heard an effeminate man saying to Abdullah bin Abu Umayyah: “If Allah enable us to conquer Ta'if tomorrow, I will show you a woman who comes in on four (roll of fat) and goes out on eight” The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Throw them out of your houses.”",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2614-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2614-muhammadfouadabdalbaqi",
          "name": "Muhammad Fouad Abd al-Baqi",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2614-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1324-20-2614-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}